WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Copper oxide is a black powder
that won't dissolve in water.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.850
But stir it into dilute
acid, and it disappears.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.130
The acid reacts with it and
turns into a solution of a salt.

4
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.970
Now here's the strange part.

5
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.870
When chemists make that salt,

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.210
they deliberately tip in more
copper oxide than can possibly

7
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.390
react.

8
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.130
Some is left over,
sitting at the bottom.

9
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.170
Why would anyone add
too much on purpose?

10
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.950
In this mission, you'll make a
soluble salt from an acid and an

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.200
insoluble base, step by step,
from mixing to crystals.

12
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.470
You'll also see which method to
use when the base dissolves.

13
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.140
Your mission: explain why
chemists add too much on purpose.
